00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:15,000
The unforgettable true story of a UFC legend.

2
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:24,000
The Smashing Machine is a history, drama film directed by Benny Safdie.

3
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:33,000
In the late 1990s, up-and-coming mixed martial artist Mark Kerr
aspires to become the greatest fighter in the world.

4
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:42,000
However, he must also battle his opioid dependence and a
volatile relationship with his girlfriend Dawn.

5
00:30:45,000 --> 00:30:51,000
Mark Kerr, played by Dwayne Johnson.

6
00:36:54,000 --> 00:37:00,000
Dawn Staples, played by Emily Blunt.

7
00:43:03,000 --> 00:43:09,000
Mark Coleman, played by Ryan Bader.

8
00:49:12,000 --> 00:49:18,000
Bas Rutten, played by Bas Rutten.

9
00:55:21,000 --> 00:55:27,000
Elizabeth Coleman, played by Lyndsey Gavin.

10
01:01:30,000 --> 01:01:36,000
McKenzie Coleman, played by Zoe Kosovic.

11
01:07:39,000 --> 01:07:45,000
The Smashing Machine is a 2025 American biographical sports drama film
written, directed, produced, and edited by Benny Safdie.

12
01:13:48,000 --> 01:13:54,000
It stars Dwayne Johnson as former amateur wrestler and MMA fighter Mark Kerr, alongside Emily Blunt as Kerr's
girlfriend Dawn Staples, with Ryan Bader, Bas Rutten and Oleksandr Usyk in supporting roles.

13
01:19:57,000 --> 01:20:03,000
The Smashing Machine premiered in the main competition of the 82nd Venice
International Film Festival on September 1, 2025, where it won the Silver Lion.

14
01:26:06,000 --> 01:26:12,000
It was released in the United States by A24 on October 3 and received generally positive reviews
from critics, with Johnson and Blunt receiving acclaim for their performances.

15
01:32:15,000 --> 01:32:21,000
The film was a box office bomb, grossing $21 million
against a $50 million production budget.

16
01:38:24,000 --> 01:38:30,000
It was nominated for the Best Makeup and Hairstyling
Award at the 98th Academy Awards.

17
01:44:33,000 --> 01:44:39,000
At the 83rd Golden Globe Awards, Johnson was nominated for Best Actor in a Motion Picture –
Drama and Blunt was nominated for Best Supporting Actress – Motion Picture.

18
01:50:42,000 --> 01:50:48,000
The film explores themes of drug addiction, biography, based on
true story, mixed martial arts (mma), price of fame.

19
01:56:51,000 --> 01:56:57,000
The tone is emotional.
